 - `GET /staff` lists the active admins and agents, oldest first, as `{id, name, role}`. Staff
   use it for assignment controls. Agents and admins can both call it.
+
+## Groups
+
+Groups are the departments the business works in, such as Billing or Technical Support. Groups
+**organize** work. They never hide tickets: every staff member can see every ticket.
+
+- **Groups** (`/api/v1/groups`). A group has `id`, `name`, `created_at` and `updated_at`. Names are
+  trimmed and required, at most 120 characters, and unique within the business, ignoring case. A
+  duplicate is `422` (`validation_failed`, with the reason under `details.name`). Staff list and
+  show groups, oldest first. Admins create, rename (`PATCH` with `name`) and delete them.
+- **Memberships** (`/api/v1/group_memberships`) put a staff member in a group. A membership has
+  `id`, `group_id`, `user_id`, `default`, `group` (`{id, name}`), `user` (`{id, name}`), `created_at`
+  and `updated_at`. Only admins and agents of the business can be members. A staff member can be in
+  several groups, but only once per group (`422`). Staff list and show memberships, oldest first,
+  and filter them with `?group_id=` and `?user_id=`. Admins add and remove them. A filter that is not
+  a whole number ID is `400 invalid_filter`.
+- **Deleting a group** removes its memberships. Its tickets become ungrouped and lose their assignee,
+  since that person was only valid in this group. Ticket `updated_at` does not change.
+- **Removing a membership** unassigns that person from the tickets in that group. The tickets stay in
+  the group. The ticket's `updated_at` does not change.
+- **Default group.** Every staff member with memberships has exactly one default. The first group a
+  staff member joins becomes their default, and `default: true` on a later membership makes that one
+  the default instead. The database enforces one default per staff member. `PUT
+  /group_memberships/:id/make_default` (admins) makes a membership the default. Removing the default
+  makes the oldest remaining membership the default. Removing the last membership leaves the staff
+  member with no default.
+- **Suspension** keeps memberships for later, and restoring a user keeps them as they were.
+  Suspension still unassigns the user's tickets, as before.
diff --git a/app/controllers/api/v1/group_memberships_controller.rb b/app/controllers/api/v1/group_memberships_controller.rb
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..3041244
--- /dev/null
+++ b/app/controllers/api/v1/group_memberships_controller.rb
@@ -0,0 +1,92 @@
+module Api
+  module V1
+    # Which staff belong to which groups. Staff can browse memberships. Admins add and remove
+    # them, and choose each staff member's default group.
+    class GroupMembershipsController < ApplicationController
+      include Pagination
+
+      before_action :authenticate_session!
+      before_action :require_active_account!
+      before_action :require_staff!
+      before_action :require_admin!, only: %i[create make_default destroy]
+      before_action :load_membership, only: %i[show make_default destroy]
+
+      # GET /api/v1/group_memberships?group_id=20&user_id=12
+      # Oldest first. Both filters are optional and combine.
+      def index
+        scope = @account.group_memberships.includes(:group, :user).order(id: :asc)
+        scope = scope.where(group_id: filter_id(:group_id)) if params[:group_id].present?
+        scope = scope.where(user_id: filter_id(:user_id)) if params[:user_id].present?
+
+        records, paging = paginate(scope)
+        render json: { group_memberships: records.map(&:as_api_json), **paging }
+      end
+
+      # GET /api/v1/group_memberships/:id
+      def show
+        render json: { group_membership: @membership.as_api_json }
+      end
+
+      # POST /api/v1/group_memberships
+      # { group_membership: { group_id: 20, user_id: 12, default: true } }
+      # The first group a staff member joins is their default, whatever default says.
+      def create
+        attrs = require_envelope(:group_membership)
+        default = attrs.key?(:default) ? parse_boolean(attrs[:default]) : false
+        if default.nil?
+          return render_error(422, "validation_failed", "default must be true or false.",
+                              details: { default: ["must be true or false"] })
+        end
+
+        group = @account.groups.find_by(id: body_id(attrs[:group_id]))
+        user = @account.users.find_by(id: body_id(attrs[:user_id]))
+        if group.nil? || user.nil?
+          details = {}
+          details[:group] = ["must be a group in this business"] if group.nil?
+          details[:user] = ["must be a user in this business"] if user.nil?
+          return render_error(422, "validation_failed", "Choose a group and a user in this business.", details: details)
+        end
+
+        membership = GroupMembership.add!(group: group, user: user, default: default)
+        render json: { group_membership: membership.as_api_json }, status: :created
+      end
+
+      # PUT /api/v1/group_memberships/:id/make_default
+      def make_default
+        @membership.make_default!
+        render json: { group_membership: @membership.as_api_json }
+      end
+
+      # DELETE /api/v1/group_memberships/:id
+      # Their tickets in this group are unassigned, and the tickets stay in the group.
+      def destroy
+        @membership.remove!
+        render json: { group_membership: @membership.as_api_json }
+      end
+
+      private
+
+      def load_membership
+        @membership = @account.group_memberships.includes(:group, :user).find_by(id: params[:id])
+        render_error(404, "not_found", "No group membership has that ID.") unless @membership
+      end
+
+      # A filter value must be a whole number ID. Anything else is a 400 invalid_filter, rather than
+      # a list that looks filtered but is not.
+      def filter_id(name)
+        value = params[name]
+        return value.to_i if value.is_a?(String) && value.match?(RequestFilter::ID_FORMAT) && value.to_i.positive?
+
+        description = name == :group_id ? "a group ID" : "a user ID"
+        raise RequestFilter::Invalid, "#{name} must be #{description}."
+      end
+
+      # A group or user ID in a body. A value that is not a whole number becomes nil, which matches
+      # no record, so it is refused like any ID outside the business.
+      def body_id(value)
+        id = parse_optional_id(value)
+        id.is_a?(Integer) ? id : nil
+      end
+    end
+  end
+end
